.\" armin(1): the manual page. install.sh copies it to
.\" ~/.local/share/man/man1; read it in place with: man ./docs/armin.1
.TH ARMIN 1 2026-10-22 armin "User Commands"
.SH NAME
armin \- a terminal coding assistant backed by llama.cpp models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B armin
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B armin
.B \-web
.I addr
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B armin
.BR \-lsp " | " \-mcp
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B armin
.B \-install
.IR org/repo [: QUANT ]
|
.I org/repo/file.gguf
|
.I file.gguf
.br
.B armin
.B \-uninstall
.IR name " | " list
.br
.B armin
.B \-library\-sync
|
.B \-library\-add
.IR path ,...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B armin
reads, searches and edits a codebase, runs its build and tests, and
grounds every answer in what is actually there. It talks to a
.BR llama-server (1)
model, local or on a remote box, or to a hosted API, and gives it a
set of narrow, structured tools \(em never a free\-form shell string
\(em jailed to the project root.
.PP
.I path
is shorthand for
.BR \-root :
.B "armin .\&"
and
.B "armin \-root .\&"
are the same, and the path may go anywhere among the flags. Giving
both is an error. With neither, the root is the current directory.
.PP
The same tool layer is served four ways:
.TP
.B REPL
The default: a chat in the terminal.
.TP
.BI \-web " addr"
The same chat in a browser on localhost, with previews for PDFs,
Markdown and code.
.TP
.B \-lsp
A Language Server on stdio, run alongside your real one: hover
explanations, ctags\-backed definitions and workspace symbols,
fill\-in\-the\-middle inline completion, and an
.B armin.ask
command. See
.I docs/nvim.md
for the Neovim client.
.TP
.B \-mcp
The tools alone, over MCP stdio, for another agent to use.
.PP
One armin serves each project: a terminal armin started where nvim's
armin already runs joins its chat instead of loading a second set of
models. Pass
.B \-new
to start a separate one.
.SH OPTIONS
Every flag's default can come from
.IR config.conf ;
a flag given on the command line wins. Flags take one dash or two.
.SS Project and model
.TP
.BI \-root " dir"
Project root; every path a tool touches is jailed to it. Default
.IR . .
.TP
.BI \-add\-dir " dir" ,...
Directories outside the project armin may read, never write, e.g.
.BR "\-add\-dir .." .
.TP
.BI \-model " name"
The chat model: a
.BI models. name
entry in
.IR config.conf ,
or, with no such entry, a label for whatever runs at
.BR \-llama\-url .
Default
.BR chat .
.TP
.BI \-llama\-url " url"
llama\-server used for a
.B \-model
with no
.BI models. name
entry. Default
.BR http://localhost:8080 .
.TP
.BI \-completion\-model " name"
The model for
.BR \-lsp 's
inline completion; should be a fill\-in\-the\-middle code model.
Default: the
.B \-model
itself.
.TP
.BI \-completion\-llama\-url " url"
Like
.BR \-llama\-url ,
for
.BR \-completion\-model .
Default: reuse
.BR \-llama\-url .
.TP
.BI \-ctags\-bin " path"
Universal Ctags binary for
.BR \-lsp 's
definitions, symbols and hover grounding. Default:
.B universal\-ctags
on
.BR PATH ,
else
.IR ~/.local/bin/universal\-ctags .
Empty disables those features.
.SS Thinking
.TP
.BI \-effort " level"
How hard the model thinks:
.B auto
(it judges each request),
.BR off ,
.BR low ,
.B medium
or
.BR high .
Default
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI \-aids " list"
Reasoning aids:
.BR all ,
.BR none ,
or a comma\-separated list of
.B stuck
(step back after repeated failures),
.B procedure
(steps per kind of task) and
.B verify
(check the work before answering). Default
.BR all .
.TP
.BI \-max\-rounds " n"
Tool\-call rounds per turn before the model must report back.
Default 50.
.SS Tools and safety
.TP
.B \-yes
Apply file writes and approve
.B run_program
runs without asking.
.BR rm ,
.BR cp ,
.BR mv ,
.B scp
and
.B rsync
are still asked every time.
.TP
.B \-dry\-run
.B run_command
describes what it would execute instead of running it.
.TP
.BI \-timeout " duration"
Per\-subprocess timeout. Default
.BR 20s .
.TP
.BI \-max\-output " bytes"
Tool output kept before truncation. Default 4000.
.SS Frontends
.TP
.BI \-web " addr"
Serve the chat in a browser at this localhost address, e.g.
.BR 127.0.0.1:7777 .
.TP
.B \-lsp
Serve hover, completion and an ask command over LSP stdio.
.TP
.B \-mcp
Serve the sandboxed tools over MCP stdio.
.TP
.B \-new
Start a separate armin even when one already serves this project.
.TP
.B \-no\-color
Disable ANSI styling.
.SS Sessions
.TP
.BR \-resume " [\fIid\fR]"
Resume a saved session: alone, pick from a menu; with an id, or a
unique prefix of one, that session, in its own project directory and
on its own model.
.TP
.B \-no\-save
Don't write the session to disk.
.SS Models
These add or remove a model, then exit; they load none.
.TP
.BI \-install " model"
Size a model up against this machine (VRAM, RAM, the context it
leaves room for), then download it and add a
.BI models. name
block to
.IR config.conf .
.I model
is
.IR org/repo [: QUANT ]
on Hugging Face,
.IR org/repo/file.gguf ,
or a
.I .gguf
already on disk.
.TP
.BI \-install\-to " dir"
Where
.B \-install
downloads. Default: where your models already are, else
.IR ~/models .
.TP
.BI \-uninstall " name"
Remove a model's
.I config.conf
lines and its
.IR .gguf ,
unless another model uses the file.
.B "\-uninstall list"
shows every model and its size.
.SS Reference library
These work on the folder named by
.B library
in
.IR config.conf ,
then exit.
.TP
.B \-library\-sync
Index the library and have
.B \-model
catalog the books the topic table lacks.
.TP
.BI \-library\-add " path" ,...
Copy files or folders into the library, then index and catalog them.
.TP
.BI \-library\-to " folder"
The library folder (topic)
.B \-library\-add
copies into. Default
.BR added .
.SH SLASH COMMANDS
Typed at the REPL prompt.
.TP
.BR /help ", " /?
List commands.
.TP
.BR /quit ", " /exit ", " /q
Leave.
.TP
.B /clear
Reset the conversation to the system prompt.
.TP
.BR /model " [\fIname\fR]"
Show the active and configured models, or switch.
.TP
.BR /effort " [\fIlevel\fR] [\fItask\fR]"
Show or set how hard the model thinks; with a task, for that task
alone.
.TP
.BR /context ", " /ctx
Messages, tool calls and an estimate of the tokens used.
.TP
.BR /compact " [\fIn\fR]"
Summarize everything but the last
.I n
messages to free context.
.TP
.B /tools
List the model's tools.
.TP
.B /root
Show the project root, timeout, allowlist and dry\-run state.
.TP
.B /history
Dump the raw conversation.
.TP
.BR /add\-dir " [\fIdir\fR]"
Let armin read a directory outside the project; alone, list them.
.TP
.BR /sessions " [rm \fIid\fR]"
List sessions, or delete one and its scratchpad.
.TP
.BI /resume " id"
Switch to another session of this directory.
.TP
.BI /title " text"
Rename this session.
.TP
.B /save
Save the session now.
.TP
.B /suggest
Toggle numbered follow\-up questions after each answer.
.TP
.B /ghosttext
Toggle ghost\-text completion while typing; Tab accepts.
.TP
.B /thinking
Toggle showing the model's thinking as it streams.
.TP
.B /approve
Toggle asking before each file write.
.TP
.BR /memory " [show|rm \fIname\fR]"
List, show or delete memories.
.TP
.BI /remember " text"
Ask the model to save something to memory.
.TP
.B /skills
List skills.
.TP
.BI /skill " name" " \fR[\fItask\fR]"
.TQ
.BI / name " \fR[\fItask\fR]"
Run a skill.
.TP
.BR /scratch " [show \fIname\fR|clear]"
List, show or clear the scratchpad.
.TP
.BR /library " [index|catalog|merge|add|topics] ..."
The reference library: status, reindex, catalog new books, copy files
in, show the topic table.
.SH LINE EDITING
On a terminal the prompt is edited in raw mode: Backspace, Ctrl\-U
clears the line, Ctrl\-W deletes a word, Ctrl\-C interrupts a running
turn, Ctrl\-D leaves. There is no cursor movement or history. Piped
input is read line by line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/armin/config.conf
.B key = value
lines and
.B #
comments. Holds every flag's default, the
.BI models. name .*
blocks (a local llama\-server to spawn and reap, a hosted API, or a
cloud machine), and agent and sandbox keys such as
.BR allow ,
.BR allow_exec ,
.BR context_size ,
.BR test_cmd ,
.B build_cmd
and
.BR library .
.TP
.I ~/.config/armin/.env
.B KEY=value
lines for API keys and cloud credentials, which
.I config.conf
names with
.B api_key_env
but never holds. armin refuses to read it when anyone but you can.
.TP
.I ~/.config/armin/skills/
.TQ
.IB project /.armin/skills/
Skills: folders holding a
.I SKILL.md
and its files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/armin/sessions/
Saved sessions, one append\-only file per session, readable by you
alone.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/armin/memory/
Memories the model saved, per project and for every project.
.TP
.IB ~/.local/share/armin/scratch/ project / session /
Each session's scratchpad: plans, findings, archived tool results.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Replaces
.I ~/.config
above.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Replaces
.I ~/.local/share
above.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables ANSI styling, as
.B \-no\-color
does.
.PP
A variable exported in the environment wins over the same key in
.IR .env .
Every command armin runs gets an environment with API keys and cloud
credentials removed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when armin fails, 2 for a command\-line error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Chat about the project in the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.B armin .\&
.RE
.PP
Use the
.B coder
model from
.IR config.conf ,
writing files without asking:
.PP
.RS
.B armin ~/code/fox \-model coder \-yes
.RE
.PP
Pick up where you left off:
.PP
.RS
.B armin \-resume 999cd437
.RE
.PP
See whether a model fits before downloading it:
.PP
.RS
.B armin \-install Qwen/Qwen3\-8B\-GGUF:Q4_K_M
.RE
.PP
The chat in a browser:
.PP
.RS
.B armin . \-web 127.0.0.1:7777
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llama-server (1),
.BR rg (1),
.BR universal-ctags (1),
.BR nvim (1)
.PP
.I README.md
covers the tools, the safety model, every config key and the model
lifecycle;
.I docs/architecture.md
the code.
